This licence covers the SpiffBoy SDK: its guide, its tools, its tests, its
development menu, its example cartridges and its exercises, in this
repository, in the Steam Workshop items that ship it, and in every copy of
them. SpiffBoy itself is covered by the SpiffBoy Licence.

The SpiffBoy SDK follows the Project Zomboid Modding Policy and the Project
Zomboid Terms and Conditions of The Indie Stone. Where this licence and them
disagree, they prevail.

1. The Indie Stone

   The Indie Stone may use, modify, reproduce, create derivative works from,
   distribute, transmit, perform, communicate and exploit the SpiffBoy SDK
   and its code, in whole or in part, in connection with Project Zomboid,
   including in the game itself, as the Project Zomboid Modding Policy
   describes.

2. Example cartridges and code samples

   The example cartridges Hello SpiffBoy and Spiff-Pong (code, art and
   texts), the exercise solutions and the code samples of the guide may be
   copied, modified and published freely, in whole or in part, in cartridge
   mods made for SpiffBoy. Credit is welcome but not required.

3. Guide, tools, tests and development menu

   a. You may read the guide, and use the tools, the tests and the
      development menu, to make, test and publish cartridge mods for
      SpiffBoy, and modify them for your own personal use.
   b. What the tools make for your cartridge (labels, art, the files of a
      new cartridge) belongs to you.
   c. Without the written permission of Ohhoop, you may not copy, upload or
      redistribute the guide, the tools, the tests or the development menu,
      including in a public or unlisted modpack, publish a modified version
      of them, or use them, or the programming interfaces of SpiffBoy they
      describe, to build or document any other console, framework or game
      system.

4. Cartridge mods

   A cartridge mod made with the SpiffBoy SDK belongs to its author. It must
   require SpiffBoy and run on it, and it must follow the Project Zomboid
   Modding Policy: it may not be sold or put behind a paywall or a
   donation.

5. Project Zomboid

   Thanks to The Indie Stone for creating Project Zomboid
